cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these maps or their data, please cite them as below."
title: "Totality Path & Nearby Locations"
abstract: >-
  Maps and data for watching total solar eclipses: every populated place in
  the path of totality, using NASA's Besselian elements. For each place the
  dataset gives the duration of totality, local times, the Sun's altitude,
  the distance from the centre line and, closer to each date, historical
  cloud cover. It covers eleven total eclipses from 2017 to 2035.
